  "description": "actix-http 3.18.10 before 3.20.2 contains an HTTP request smuggling vulnerability in its chunked decoder, which treats a bare LF after the last chunk as the start of a trailer section. Attackers can send a body ending in 0\\r\\n\\n through a connection-reusing proxy so the next request's body is parsed as new requests, bypassing WAF or upstream protections.",
